# Tests skipped on OpenBSD (one name per line; "#" starts a comment). The
# test binary embeds this file and sets -test.skip from it on OpenBSD, unless
# -test.skip is given or E2E_OPENBSD_ALL=1 (platform_skip_test.go).
#
# OpenBSD has no unified buffer cache: data written with write()/pwrite() is
# not seen through another process's MAP_SHARED mapping of the same file, so
# Diablo's readers of the history, KPDB (dactive.kp) and overview files see
# stale data there (ISSUES.md D-171). Supporting it would need a design
# change, which the maintainer decided against (2026-11-03). These are the
# tests that fail on OpenBSD 7.9 for that reason, from the CI run of #272
# (96a15fb), plus TestPipeliningFeederStreaming (a CHECK right after its
# TAKETHIS misses the history entry; seen on #273) and TestHistoryReopenAfterSwap
# (#279: the first add is not seen through the map).
